              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent (Curtis E. Gannon), according to Respondent (Curtis E. Gannon), when a criminal defendant and the government agree to a specific sentence and that agreement is binding on the sentencing judge by virtue of Rule 11(c)(1)(C), the resulting sentence is based on the parties' agreement, not on the advisory guideline range."
